# The root Caddyfile on the Ampere box — /etc/caddy/Caddyfile.
#
# Deliberately almost empty. The whole MonkeyHub site block lives in
# hosting/caddy-monkeyhub.conf and is installed alongside this file as
# /etc/caddy/monkeyhub.conf by `./deploy.sh --infra`, which validates the merged
# config before it reloads. Edit the site THERE, not here and not on the box.
#
# `deploy.sh --infra` greps this file for the import line below and refuses to
# run without it, so keep it.
#
# Unlike the old VPS's Caddyfile this has no nestzone block: nestzone and
# couplezone stay on 79.76.54.204, which is still their box.
#
# Caddy therefore listens on :8081 only — no :80, no :443, no certificates to
# manage. Everything public arrives through cloudflared, which dials out, so
# this box needs no inbound port beyond SSH and no Oracle security-list change.

import monkeyhub.conf
